{"version":"2026.10.11-r25","id":"Q410772","formula":"C₂Cl₄","hill":"C2Cl4","elements":["C","Cl"],"composition":{"C":2.0,"Cl":4.0},"names":{"en":"Tetrachloroethylene","ru":"Тетрахлорэтилен","uk":"Тетрахлоретилен"},"descriptions":{"en":"Tetrachloroethylene, also known as perchloroethylene or under the systematic name tetrachloroethene, and abbreviations such as perc, and PCE, is a chlorocarbon with the formula Cl2C=CCl2. It is a volatile, non-flammable, stable, colorless and dense liquid widely used for dry cleaning of fabrics and as a metal degreasing solvent, formerly as an oral anthelmintic. It has a mild, sweet, sharp odor, detectable by most people at a concentration of 50 ppm.","ru":"Тетрахлорэтилен (перхлорэтилен) — бесцветная жидкость с резким запахом, хлорорганический растворитель. Широкое применение находит в химчистке и обезжиривании металлов."},"fame":35,"pubchemCid":31373,"mass":165.8,"charge":0,"smiles":"C(=C(Cl)Cl)(Cl)Cl","inchikey":"CYTYCFOTNPOANT-UHFFFAOYSA-N","iupac":"1,1,2,2-tetrachloroethene","classes":[{"qid":"Q113145171","names":{"en":"type of chemical entity","ru":"тип химического объекта","uk":"тип хімічної сутності"}}],"structureInfo":{"kind":"molecule","source":"pubchem","ref":"31373","atoms":6,"license":"PubChem (NIH), public data"},"structure":{"kind":"molecule","atoms":[{"x":-1.606,"y":-1.464,"z":0.0,"el":"Cl"},{"x":-1.606,"y":1.464,"z":0.0,"el":"Cl"},{"x":1.606,"y":1.465,"z":0.0,"el":"Cl"},{"x":1.606,"y":-1.464,"z":0.0,"el":"Cl"},{"x":-0.672,"y":0.0,"z":0.0,"el":"C"},{"x":0.672,"y":0.0,"z":0.0,"el":"C"}],"bonds":[[0,4,1],[1,4,1],[2,5,1],[3,5,1],[4,5,2]]},"sources":[{"role":"identity","name":"Wikidata","url":"https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q410772","license":"CC0 1.0"},{"role":"description","name":"Wikipedia (en)","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tetrachloroethylene","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"role":"description","name":"Wikipedia (ru)","url":"https://ru.wikipedia.org/wiki/%D0%A2%D0%B5%D1%82%D1%80%D0%B0%D1%85%D0%BB%D0%BE%D1%80%D1%8D%D